identifier: kgmicrobe.ingredient:jcm414_calcium_magnesium_trace_solution
preferred_term: JCM 414 calcium-magnesium trace-metal preparation
ingredient_type: STOCK_SOLUTION
mapping_status: MAPPED
ontology_mapping:
  ontology_id: kgmicrobe.ingredient:jcm414_calcium_magnesium_trace_solution
  ontology_label: JCM 414 calcium-magnesium trace-metal preparation
  ontology_source: kgmicrobe.ingredient
  mapping_quality: FALLBACK_REGISTRY
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: CURATOR_JUDGMENT
    source: https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=414; https://togomedium.org/medium/M412
    notes: 'JCM414 explicitly dissolves calcium and magnesium salts plus its trace-metal
      solution separately from the phosphate/thiosulfate preparation. This is a physical
      premix; 460 ml is the added water volume. Source transcription basis (literal
      input amounts, not calculated stock concentrations): Distilled water: 460 ml;
      CaCl2・2H2O: 0.1 g; MgCl2・6H2O: 0.2 g; Trace metal solution (see below): 1 ml.
      No batch-to-final-volume conversion is made. Handling atmosphere is not listed
      as a material part; pH reagents are source inputs, without an assertion of unchanged
      molecular species after pH adjustment. Nested formulations remain source-qualified
      named parts where exact composition/owner identity is not established. No verified
      exact eligible ontology term or existing whole-preparation owner was established
      by the bounded source/owner review. This self-registry mapping represents the
      preparation, not its individual constituents.'
